    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0774" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/4–1749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-21T13:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>703. For Parker from Treasury. Reurtel 1215<anchor n="59" xml:id="d719-f1"/>
                    FRBNY advised April 21 sell 100,000 ounces gold to Chicenbank. Received Toeca
                        1345<anchor n="60" xml:id="d719-f2"/> advise ChiGovt informally and orally
                    that it may rely upon availability gold for future purchases its Central Bank to
                    replenish outlays for purchase tin for delivery under existing arrangements
                    R.F.C. Advise Green[e].<anchor n="61" xml:id="d719-f3"/> State and ECA concur
                    all above. [Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
